#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119687 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "85acf106-2f03-5509-8ad0-08b82ef2a4c6" :question/math-academy-id "e-8005" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n![](images/1f/1fd9cafe0db4412b48885cebacd68b9866a79fadfdb7767c3b63f8469d31bfea.svg)\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of $a_{31}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4 \\times 4$ determinant to a $3 \\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of $a_{31}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+3{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-3){C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -5 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =4(11-3) \\\\  & =32.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119690 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "4a9954b2-3d4b-5669-88cd-6e74c9683a60" :question/math-academy-id "e-8054" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Find a $3\\times 3$ determinant that has the same value.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below $a_{11}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries below $a_{11}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 5 & -7 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3 & -4\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & -1 & -9 \\\\ -10 & -8 & -9 \\\\ 9 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119691 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "ccf558b9-bf00-58c7-b244-2c5797f93d8e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8060" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Find a $3\\times 3$ determinant that has the same value.\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of $a_{23}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (or column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ -4 & -4 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+3{C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 3 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+3}|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -10 & 11\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54bddb8d-cf36-57d3-8990-5419840cdebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}8 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & -7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -14 & 19\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440743} {:answer/id #uuid "c076c4ac-c079-5402-8162-3e9e7e97c4a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}13 & -8 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ -4 & 6 & 12\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440753} {:answer/id #uuid "df6a56d6-11e4-5ce2-b833-c8b6d50c3e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}13 & 10 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -16 & -21\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440762} {:answer/id #uuid "f439f4fb-9730-5674-820b-040ca58a4b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440764} {:answer/id #uuid "f563015d-cc65-5533-8c04-fd6a642474d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 10 & 2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -13 & 24\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f439f4fb-9730-5674-820b-040ca58a4b57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440764} :answer-field/id #uuid "5017e5ab-f540-5f24-b47d-7ab195cf9ff0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1c17071-3f38-5e15-9f1d-979ec9d512e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-131226" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above ${a}_{42}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above ${a}_{42}=1$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 3 & -7 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{4} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}13 & 0 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 0 & -16 & 21 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 3 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+2}|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}13 & 11 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -16 & 21\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440779 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476634a7-3127-5dfb-8548-86988b800729" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440740} {:answer/id #uuid "8677367f-731e-5786-810b-4a5834eb9e63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -8 \\\\ -6 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440747} {:answer/id #uuid "c5998369-5efd-53c2-a6dc-3f4d2c8c17c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 2 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 9 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440755} {:answer/id #uuid "fb266362-88fb-55ee-b32a-0a37bb635c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440767} {:answer/id #uuid "ffc76282-8435-5ff8-9828-1f03763d49b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -10 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440768}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb266362-88fb-55ee-b32a-0a37bb635c10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440767} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fccaa80-3817-5c7f-a05e-83fa6ed0c12d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440773}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4d57bf97-1629-5c5b-aa31-076c598fe8ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-131255" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries above and below ${a}_{22}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries above and below ${a}_{22}=2$ equal to zero using elementary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 & -11 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & -2 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 0 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 8 & 0 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-7 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 8 & -11 & -3 \\\\ -6 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440780 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24b9de88-7ddb-5b58-b30d-923571de9446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 7 & 1 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 10 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440736} {:answer/id #uuid "78242538-3ed6-59de-be3c-33fa32cdeeb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440745} {:answer/id #uuid "c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440754} {:answer/id #uuid "d00d7ab2-12e5-5af5-a41f-707d9c669240" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 \\\\ -3 & -12 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440756} {:answer/id #uuid "d0a38a5e-bb09-5bb9-acfc-39240d600c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 7 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 5 & -8\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440757}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4eb8721-33ec-52bc-8a6e-8bb24d93b164" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440754} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6055d74-81b9-54e0-8fc3-55044161a211" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51f6ebb7-f4d6-54f8-92af-8a0f13b34712" :question/math-academy-id "q-132020" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 12 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & 6 & 12 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -8 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 5 & -6\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 5 & -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 7 & 1 & -4 \\\\ -8 & -10 & 4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266147 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10b024a3-fa6e-5a50-9629-99ef7def6fa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263154} {:answer/id #uuid "3765d51c-d5ac-519a-9e70-5cd93e1c8ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "414" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263497} {:answer/id #uuid "6298a35d-c73e-5280-8353-3dc2e6fba29d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "298" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263849} {:answer/id #uuid "ca000009-455a-58b7-9c8d-de3f64fdc56b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "531" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264766} {:answer/id #uuid "ffbfdd21-cacf-55dc-9222-240b2a07e47e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "378" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265249}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3765d51c-d5ac-519a-9e70-5cd93e1c8ff7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "414" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263497} :answer-field/id #uuid "6eb1dbd9-5423-5c3a-8e04-931fffbce60e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265434}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d00f5bdf-fb0f-57e8-b395-12f0570296a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-132163" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 10 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -8 & -2\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{11}=3$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 & -6 & -3 \\\\ -5 & -6 & 10 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 8 & -8 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot (3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}9 & 7 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9(18+28) \\\\  & =9(46) \\\\  & =414.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120419 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89a9045a-7bce-5521-9e5e-c18cda1bc188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118629} {:answer/id #uuid "1428c966-b14f-5658-a6f5-11220376879d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118630} {:answer/id #uuid "2370d1bf-4d63-5ef2-82b0-1bf300a84b77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118631} {:answer/id #uuid "47b9c8a5-e5a1-5b17-a0a2-47a2f155c5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118632} {:answer/id #uuid "5f193840-cca0-5ffb-95a1-ae4e4782955b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47b9c8a5-e5a1-5b17-a0a2-47a2f155c5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118632} :answer-field/id #uuid "67dfd6a1-fb8e-5c81-a959-a13da9e1b424" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118628}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "150c328e-7322-5fa3-b605-dd458b140db6" :question/math-academy-id "q-42075" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary row operations to make the entries below ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary row operations, let's make entries below ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-(4-(-2)) \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394840 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119874 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b0edd60-2801-59d3-b9df-18bfbf8763bb" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1de9bc2-0f30-517a-9782-a9ca1f325ab2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}11 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394842} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac6aa15-7074-542e-a631-82d70b92d723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :an