ary row operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 5 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd column, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 0 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}11 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}11 & 17 & 11 \\\\ -6 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 11 & 7 & 7\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46cd8000-1e23-5199-b2db-301eb99e864d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -7\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394862} {:answer/id #uuid "1289a79f-f03a-57c5-80ce-7fd42973e8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394863} {:answer/id #uuid "7a2989e5-bdd3-537a-85ba-5abd1555a897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394864} {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f37a-c44f-5c54-9e1a-bd783a206783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} {:answer/id #uuid "c2ae3856-08c7-541a-9fe1-12f594788fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dd0f37a-c44f-5c54-9e1a-bd783a206783" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394865} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b8b159e-b89f-5a64-b5d5-e5aa63c40762" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2a2b160-a569-5696-8596-179bbcebb9ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-91220" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left and to the right of ${a}_{33}=2$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3 & -2 & -3\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-3){C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{3} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+(-1){C}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $3$rd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 8 & -7 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119875 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "01ff3b37-83e6-506a-a6e8-07858a2bcb66" :knowledge-point/title "Reducing a 4x4 Determinant to a 3x3 Determinant Using Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "086baf34-04b6-58fc-b9f8-cd256a0f2e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 5\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354739} {:answer/id #uuid "3456bcab-7477-5733-9df3-89b18380c3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355127} {:answer/id #uuid "424cdac0-33e0-589e-94e9-d123e607def9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355250} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc929ce-9e29-5c94-bc6a-5cbf8f8914e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355906} {:answer/id #uuid "aebbe85d-89ff-5c2d-9a47-bea4603e6c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3456bcab-7477-5733-9df3-89b18380c3e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355127} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a9facd9-8b32-5537-b94e-bb833971bbbe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a551105-1281-563b-9139-cdf718553556" :question/math-academy-id "q-91221" :question/problem "$$\n|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|\n$$\n\nConsider the above $4\\times 4$ determinant. Which of the following $3\\times 3$ determinants has the same value?\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the left of ${a}_{44}$ equal to zero.*" :question/worked-solution "Let's make entries to the left of ${a}_{44}=1$ equal to zero using elementary column operations.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:={C}_{1}+(-4){C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+2{C}_{4} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{4}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $4$th row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{4+4}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -10 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dc27e22-d687-533a-9a5a-f8ec0e2b1bdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354793} {:answer/id #uuid "85ca94ec-7195-5aa1-bbbd-cc72022d704a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "33" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355843} {:answer/id #uuid "a3a1b26f-a343-5137-9997-11acffc2bef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356115} {:answer/id #uuid "cbe1bea9-6907-59a2-b366-e66cbf9da2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356443} {:answer/id #uuid "fa70dd31-26d4-5dea-9543-934d2d9ce29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa70dd31-26d4-5dea-9543-934d2d9ce29a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356854} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bae90e8-c7ce-52ff-a590-5fbc1f33fd7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9f5a627e-5fd5-5321-b04e-df13a3c56af4" :question/math-academy-id "q-91229" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{21}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{21}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2 & -2\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $2$nd row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{2+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(-6-5) \\\\  & =-22.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186440778 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119870 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37209e5f-a6e8-55d5-b76f-19f79db67566" :knowledge-point/title "Computing 4x4 Determinants Using Row and Column Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d041347-974c-5211-8af3-0d1eb0d54714" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440748} {:answer/id #uuid "a328cadc-7951-533e-ad43-d926e5950f13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440750} {:answer/id #uuid "d15147b2-fac5-5c6f-b4db-ec70e4487643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440758} {:answer/id #uuid "d2a376ea-df94-535c-826d-ac17d1f3a3ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440759} {:answer/id #uuid "e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440763}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e73e510a-6138-525f-beef-ac3b1cf34f5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "126" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440763} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb0d831e-6e0f-59da-ab3f-8c9921b69fc6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440775}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3010fec5-ce32-5d13-98b7-fb9085f51f6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-91252" :question/problem "Calculate the value of \n$\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{aligned}|.$\n\n*Hint: Use elementary column operations to make the entries to the right of ${a}_{11}$ equal to zero. You should be able to reduce the given $4\\times 4$ determinant to a $3\\times 3$ determinant.*" :question/worked-solution "Using elementary column operations, let's make entries to the right of ${a}_{11}=1$ equal to zero.\n\nSince adding a multiple of one row (or column) to another row (column) in a matrix does not change the value of its determinant, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -9 & 5\\end{aligned}| &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{C}_{2}:={C}_{2}+(-2){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{3}:={C}_{3}+(-3){C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{4}:={C}_{4}+2{C}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the result along the $1$st row, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-1)^{1+1}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot (-1)^{2+2}|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 9 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3(3-45) \\\\  & =126.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
